    "title": "A=1 quadratic center-disjoint heavy-row nonzero scalar",
    "status": "PROVED",
    "closure": "local resultant and first-jet exclusion of the zero heavy row",
    "statement": "On the separated double-root extremal locus with gcd(Lambda,g_*S_B^2)=1, the heavy row is G(t,x_*)=c g_*S_B^2 with c nonzero. If c were zero, X-x_* would divide G. At a correction root, an unsupported slope would force resultant order at least three against the exact order two; an actual-support root would violate first-jet transversality; and a padding root would put the correction slope in g_*, contradicting gcd(g_*,S_B)=1. Hence the barycentric extrapolation must equal a nonzero, not merely possibly zero, scalar multiple of g_*S_B^2.",
